{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790976749,"nonce":"sPQIJJMCh1ccu0x0v3FFknipPLA=","message":"Diagnosed on the code as it was (68d6ed36), with a test driving the list page the way a terminal does.\n\nThe unbound `rank` was the whole of it. Nothing else was wrong:\n\n- the cursor does start on the id column (`column` is 0 on a new page);\n- `Space` on the id does route to `startGrab` (`listPage.edit` sends column 0 there), and the chord is the one `?` shows;\n- with `{\"rank\":\"rank\"}` bound, the grab, the drag and the drop all worked: `space` grabbed, `down` moved the row, `space` dropped it and the rank was written;\n- the status line did not lie either, because `hintLine` already left `space: grab` out while no rank was bound — so the only thing a person saw was `enter: open · ? keys`, the bell, and `no rank: cannot reorder`.\n\nWith `rank` unbound, `startGrab` refused by design: the order was the query's and a move had nowhere to be written. The recipes in AGENTS.md never bound it, so the tracker's own list was never draggable.\n\nFixed by the decision in e524644 (3797a951): `rank` is a built-in field on every type and the view argument's default, so `startGrab` cannot be refused any more and the three \"no rank: cannot reorder\" paths are gone, on the list, the board and the gantt.\n\nOne consequence to know about, recorded in the decision: on a store where nothing has a rank yet — this one — the first drop puts its issue at the top of its group, because it is then the only issue with a rank and a null rank sorts last. Every drag after that behaves as expected. The fix for it, if it ever annoys anybody, is the order-preserving renumber the `rank` package already describes, not a different sort rule.","files":null}]}